<p>OpenAI is testing a new advertising format inside ChatGPT that goes beyond a normal click-through banner. On September 16, 2026, the company announced Sponsored Agents, a clearly labeled conversation that users can start with a business-sponsored agent after interacting with an ad. OpenAI is also adding AI tools for campaign creation, creative assistance, and integrations with HubSpot and Shopify.</p>
<figure class="article-image"><img src="/assets/images/blog/chatgpt-sponsored-agents-ads-explained.svg" width="1200" height="630" alt="ChatGPT Sponsored Agents flow from ad to labeled business conversation"></figure>
<h2>What is a Sponsored Agent?</h2>
<p>A Sponsored Agent is a business-sponsored conversation that a user can choose to open after seeing a relevant ad. OpenAI says the agent is clearly labeled and is separate from ChatGPT’s independent answers and separate from the original conversation the user started.</p>
<p>The design changes the job of the ad. Instead of ending at a landing page, the sponsored experience can answer follow-up questions, help a user explore an offer and then link to the business site when the user is ready to continue.</p>
<h2>How the new ad flow works</h2>
<ol><li>A user sees a relevant ChatGPT ad.</li><li>The user can choose to open a clearly labeled Sponsored Agent.</li><li>The user asks follow-up questions in a business-sponsored conversation.</li><li>The user can follow a link to the advertiser’s website for the next step.</li></ol>
<p>OpenAI says the sponsored conversation is distinct from ChatGPT’s independent answers. That separation is important because users should be able to tell when a response comes from a sponsored business experience rather than the general assistant.</p>
<h2>What marketers can now do with AI</h2>
<p>OpenAI is also rolling out more direct AI assistance for advertisers. Advertisers can use natural-language prompts to create, update and analyze campaigns through ChatGPT with its Ads Manager integration. The system can turn a website or brief into campaign material, review performance and suggest next actions.</p>
<p>Within Ads Manager, OpenAI says advertisers can also receive suggested copy and imagery based on the landing page and campaign objective. Advertisers can review and edit those suggestions before adding them to a campaign. Optional text customization can adapt ad copy to conversation context and translate it into a user’s preferred language.</p>
<h2>Why HubSpot and Shopify integrations matter</h2>
<p>The new integrations reduce the need to create a separate process for every advertising channel. OpenAI says HubSpot users can connect a ChatGPT Ads account, create ads, track performance and follow up on leads directly in HubSpot using HubSpot context.</p>
<p>US-based Shopify merchants can use the ChatGPT Ads app in Shopify to create and manage campaigns, with products already integrated through Shopify Catalog. OpenAI says international availability will start on September 23 in markets where ChatGPT Ads are available.</p>
<h2>What changes for search and content teams</h2>
<p>For marketers, the important shift is from a simple “ad to page” model toward an “ad to conversation to action” model. That makes product information more important because the sponsored agent needs useful source material to handle follow-up questions.</p>
<p>Content teams should keep product facts, comparison points, policies, pricing conditions and common questions easy to verify. They should also track where the user leaves the sponsored conversation, since a click is no longer the only meaningful step.</p>
<h2>What should be measured?</h2>
<table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Stage</th><th>Example metric</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Ad exposure</td><td>Impressions and engagement</td></tr><tr><td>Sponsored conversation</td><td>Conversation starts and completed interactions</td></tr><tr><td>Consideration</td><td>Qualified questions, product views or site visits</td></tr><tr><td>Business outcome</td><td>Lead, purchase or other defined conversion</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>This is still an emerging format, so teams should treat early measurements as experiments. A higher conversation rate does not automatically mean a better business result. The right baseline depends on the product, audience, sales cycle and conversion path.</p>
<h2>What remains limited or uncertain</h2>
<p>OpenAI says Sponsored Agents are being tested with select advertisers in the United States. That means the format is not a general capability for every advertiser. OpenAI has also not published a universal benchmark showing how Sponsored Agents perform against normal ad formats.</p>
<p>For marketers, the useful approach is to test the full path rather than assume the new interface will automatically improve conversion. Measure cost, conversation quality, downstream actions and business outcomes separately.</p>
<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Are Sponsored Agents the same as normal ChatGPT answers?</h3><p>No. OpenAI says the sponsored conversation is clearly labeled and separate from ChatGPT’s independent answers and the user’s original conversation.</p><h3>Can users ask Sponsored Agents follow-up questions?</h3><p>Yes. OpenAI describes the format as a business-sponsored conversation where users can ask questions, explore an offering and then follow a link to the business website.</p><h3>Is Sponsored Agents available to every advertiser?</h3><p>No. As of the announcement, OpenAI says Sponsored Agents are being tested with select advertisers in the United States.</p>
